  "problem": "Calculate ${f}^{″}(0).$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${f}^{″}(0)\\,\\,=\\,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "To find an expression for the second derivative, we differentiate the equation with respect to $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}) \\\\ \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =2x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}+\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x) \\\\  & =2x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{2xy}{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute the given expression for $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ into the above and simplify the resulting expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =-\\frac{2xy}{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\cdot 2x\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}+2\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =-4{x}^{2}y+2\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the point $(0,0)$ lies on $f,$ we substitute the coordinates of our point into the above expression for the second derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}|}_{(0,0)} & =-4\\cdot {0}^{2}\\cdot 0+2\\sqrt{1-{0}^{2}}=2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
